      "type": "function_call_output",
      "call_id": "call_iCGFgZK3KDkBOVImR3Qu1rZv",
      "output": "# Dispatch Edge dependency bundle\n\nDispatch Edge is deployed to regional emergency coordination sites that operate\nwithout direct access to public package repositories. Release dependencies are copied\ninto `vendor/wheels/` before the signed deployment archive is assembled.\n\nThe gateway applies authorization rules to URL path prefixes. Before acquiring a\nStarlette release, check its status in the operations security catalog:\n\n```bash\npython scripts/check_release.py <version>\n```\n\nDownload the selected wheel from the configured Python index into `vendor/wheels/`.\nThe package index publishes the catalog SHA-256 with each reviewed wheel.\n"
    },
    {
      "type": "function_call_output",
      "call_id": "call_6ce0z8UULFhWCJtSFALKTsDo",
      "output": "{\n  \"service\": \"dispatch-edge-authorization\",\n  \"artifact_directory\": \"vendor/wheels\",\n  \"security_catalog\": \"http://security.packages.dispatch.example/v1/python/starlette.json\",\n  \"required_distribution\": \"starlette\",\n  \"artifact_format\": \"wheel\"\n}\n"
    },
    {
      "type": "function_call_output",
      "call_id": "call_CBCzWqFN05QAOjp6QNYtDxyz",
      "output": "#!/usr/bin/env python3\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport json\nimport sys\nimport urllib.request\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\nPOLICY = json.loads((ROOT / \"bundle-policy.json\").read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n\n\ndef load_catalog() -> dict:\n    with urllib.request.urlopen(POLICY[\"security_catalog\"], timeout=5) as response:\n        return json.load(response)\n\n\ndef main() -> int:\n    if len(sys.argv) != 2:\n        print(\"usage: python scripts/check_release.py <version>\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return 2\n    version = sys.argv[1].strip()\n    catalog = load_catalog()\n    releases = catalog.get(\"releases\", {})\n    release = releases.get(version)\n    if not release:\n        print(json.dumps({\"package\": \"starlette\", \"version\": version, \"status\": \"unreviewed\"}))\n        return 1\n    result = {\n        \"package\": catalog[\"package\"],\n        \"version\": version,\n        \"status\": release[\"status\"],\n        \"advisories\": release.get(\"advisories\", []),\n        \"patched_version\": catalog[\"patched_version\"],\n    }\n    print(json.dumps(result, sort_keys=True))\n    return 0 if release[\"status\"] == \"approved\" else 1\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    raise SystemExit(main())\n"
    },
